 "social": {
  "caption": "Three myths about Japanese words for plans, promises and habits. Busted.\n\nMyth 1: 予約 (よやく) is a promise. No, it is a reservation. A promise to a person is 約束 (やくそく).\n\nMyth 2: 計画 (けいかく) and 予定 (よてい) are the same. 予定 is what is already on your schedule. 計画 is a plan you build.\n\nMyth 3: 続く (つづく) and 続ける (つづける) are the same. 続く happens by itself, like rain. 続ける is you keeping it going, like studying every day.\n\nA booking is not a promise, and a schedule is not a plan.\n\nFollow for one Japanese tip every day.",
  "hashtags": "#LearnJapanese #JapaneseVocabulary #JapaneseLanguage #JLPT #Japanese"
 },
